wr-template
===========

This layer provides template processing support for OpenEmbedded.  Wind River
templates are a mechanism that permit various configurations to be enabled
with a simple setting.

The implementation uses bitbake's native config fragment support as the
backend.  WRTEMPLATE values are mapped to OE_FRAGMENTS values, so users can
continue to use WRTEMPLATE in the same way as before.


What is a template?
-------------------
A template lives in the 'conf/fragments' directory of a given layer.  The
conf/fragments directory contains a series of directories to organize the
templates.  The name of the directory is used to enable the template.

A template directory may contain:
   README - a template README file
   <name>.conf - a configuration fragment (where <name> is the directory's
                 basename, e.g. conf/fragments/feature/foo/foo.conf)
   require - a list of other templates required for this one

The require file may include comments, starting with a '#' or template names
to include.  Circular dependencies are handled gracefully and duplicate
entries are avoided.

BSP layers can provide a default configuration fragment at
<layer>/conf/fragments/default/bsp.conf.  This fragment is automatically
loaded when the MACHINE is defined in that layer, providing BSP-specific
default configuration.  The BSP_FRAGMENTS variable controls this and can
be overridden if needed.

In addition, the layer allows the templates to set various banner messages.

    CONFIG_BANNER[path_to_template] = "..."
    BANNER[path_to_template] = "..."

A configuration banner is only displayed if bitbake has to reparse the
configuration.  A runtime banner will always be displayed when a 
build is run.


Old template format deprecation
--------------------------------
The old template format (using a 'templates' directory with template.conf,
image.inc, bsp-pkgs.conf, bsp-pkgs.inc, and README files) is deprecated.
If a layer still contains old-format templates, a fatal error will be raised
during configuration parsing.  To convert old templates to the new format, run:

    layers/wrlinux/scripts/convert-to-fragments.py <layer>

To temporarily suppress the error for specific layers, set:

    LAYERS_SKIP_OLD_TEMPLATE_CHECKING = "layerid1 layerid2"


Dependencies
------------
This layer depends on oe-core.


Maintenance
-----------
This layer is maintained by Wind River Systems, Inc.
Contact <support@windriver.com> or your support representative for more
information on submitting changes.


Building the wr-template layer
-----------------------------------
This layer should be added to the bblayers.conf file.


